## Change review - 2026-10-28

**Partial block rendering has an explicit completion boundary and stricter undefined values.** Reviewed commit `ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d` (commit date `2026-10-27T14:27:32+01:00`). Compared with `6ead3c0ffa1e731f58694f94130253a559da68f4`; the complete Git comparison contains 13 changed paths.

The interpreter now records block_captured, temporarily detaches enclosing capture buffers, restores state and returns immediately after the requested block, including propagation through super(). The render_block API documentation explicitly says later template content is not evaluated; fixtures exercise blocks inside filter/set captures, inheritance and an undefined variable after versus inside the selected block. String coercion rejects Undefined rather than converting it to empty text, with safe-filter regression cases. Arithmetic changes make integer/float floor division and modulo follow negative-infinity/divisor-sign semantics, with mixed-sign fixtures. HTML escaping writes unchanged byte runs in chunks while preserving escaped punctuation and Unicode fixtures. Unique uses hashable keys for strings/integral numbers and a separate linear fallback for maps/arrays/non-integral or oversized numbers; this is not a universal linear-time bound.

Evidence: [tera/src/vm/interpreter.rs:481-513](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/vm/interpreter.rs#L481-L513) · [tera/src/vm/interpreter.rs:574-606](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/vm/interpreter.rs#L574-L606) · [tera/src/vm/state.rs:39-95](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/vm/state.rs#L39-L95) · [tera/src/tera.rs:1469-1530](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/tera.rs#L1469-L1530) · [tera/src/tera.rs:2020-2121](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/tera.rs#L2020-L2121) · [tera/src/args.rs:199-210](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/args.rs#L199-L210) · [tera/tests/undefined.rs:1-52](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/tests/undefined.rs#L1-L52) · [tera/src/value/number.rs:145-230](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/value/number.rs#L145-L230) · [tera/src/value/number.rs:315-337](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/value/number.rs#L315-L337) · [tera/src/utils.rs:112-161](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/utils.rs#L112-L161) · [tera/src/filters.rs:612-658](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/filters.rs#L612-L658) · [tera/src/filters.rs:823-842](https://github.com/Keats/tera/blob/ad95994b2c19edcae8ddc0b98dcb8137cceed58d/tera/src/filters.rs#L823-L842).

**Harness consequence:** Generated-fragment verification must distinguish successful selected-block rendering from validity of the complete artifact. Preserve missing-data errors across convenience filters, and add numeric-sign/Unicode fixtures when swapping a renderer. Keep trusted templates separate from untrusted data and retain resource bounds for fallback comparisons; these changes do not make Tera an isolation mechanism or justify moving generation into the portable domain.

**Scope and limits:** Static review of changed renderer/argument/arithmetic/escaping/deduplication hunks and associated fixtures within a 13-path comparison. No Rust build, template execution, performance measurement or hostile-template resource test ran; unchanged VM operations and feature-dependent escape implementation were not audited.

